1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Water enters concrete through cracks and joints.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,400
Carbon dioxide advances through the cover.

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:10,000
At the rebar, corrosion follows, and the surface spalls.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,500
Sun and temperature cycles work on exposed surfaces.

5
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:16,885
A building has seven places that need protection.

6
00:00:16,885 --> 00:00:19,000
Each has its own products.

7
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:19,833
Below ground:

8
00:00:19,833 --> 00:00:21,500
raft, walls, lift pits.

9
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:24,000
Roofs and podium decks.

10
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,500
Wet areas and balconies.

11
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:29,000
Water tanks and water-retaining structures.

12
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,500
Joints and penetrations.

13
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:34,000
Façades and exposed concrete.

14
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,500
Steel and industrial exposure.

15
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:39,167
Zone A:

16
00:00:39,167 --> 00:00:40,000
below-grade.

17
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Below ground, water presses on walls and slabs.

18
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:44,875
Candidate products:

19
00:00:44,875 --> 00:00:47,500
DonProof FB, DonProof FB-S, DonProof HS.

20
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:51,000
Membrane on blinding, over a geotextile cushion;

21
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,500
concrete is cast against it.

22
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:58,000
Base fillet, minimum overlap, staggered roll ends.

23
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:03,500
FB and FB-S report the same tests, so they compare directly.

24
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:03,944
FB-S:

25
00:01:03,944 --> 00:01:05,278
pre- or post-applied.

26
00:01:05,278 --> 00:01:05,722
HS:

27
00:01:05,722 --> 00:01:07,500
no priming or fillets.

28
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:08,333
Zone B:

29
00:01:08,333 --> 00:01:10,000
roofs and podium decks.

30
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:14,000
On roofs, the surface sees rain, sun and foot traffic.

31
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:14,875
Candidate products:

32
00:01:14,875 --> 00:01:17,500
DonProof PU-P150, DonProof PU-P100, DonProof PU-P60.

33
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:23,500
Primed deck, hot-sprayed polyurea, then an aliphatic polyurethane topcoat.

34
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:26,312
Spray perpendicular to the substrate;

35
00:01:26,312 --> 00:01:28,000
strip-coat internal corners.

36
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,500
All three report tensile, elongation and tear to the same ASTM methods.

37
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:33,909
P150:

38
00:01:33,909 --> 00:01:35,545
inverted roofs under XPS.

39
00:01:35,545 --> 00:01:35,955
P60:

40
00:01:35,955 --> 00:01:38,000
cold resistance to minus forty.

41
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:38,833
Zone C:

42
00:01:38,833 --> 00:01:40,500
wet areas and balconies.

43
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:44,500
In wet areas, water sits on the surface.

44
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:45,375
Candidate products:

45
00:01:45,375 --> 00:01:48,000
DonProof PU-C100, Aquathane R100, Aquathane E400.

46
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Primer, membrane in one or two coats, then the tile finish.

47
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Corner fillet, reinforcing strip at changes of plane, recoat within 24 hours.

48
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:04,500
Bond to concrete is reported to the same ASTM method.

49
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:04,917
C100:

50
00:02:04,917 --> 00:02:08,250
cold applied by roller, brush, trowel or squeegee.

51
00:02:08,250 --> 00:02:08,667
E400:

52
00:02:08,667 --> 00:02:09,500
under tiles.

53
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:10,333
Zone D:

54
00:02:10,333 --> 00:02:12,000
tanks and water-retaining structures.

55
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Tanks hold water against the lining.

56
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:16,875
Candidate products:

57
00:02:16,875 --> 00:02:19,500
Strongcoat EPW-P, Strongcoat EPW-S, Setseal 300C.

58
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:25,500
Two coats of Strongcoat EPW on the concrete wall.

59
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:28,833
Second coat within 24 hours at 25 degrees;

60
00:02:28,833 --> 00:02:30,500
never over standing water.

61
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:32,944
One TDS, two grades:

62
00:02:32,944 --> 00:02:36,000
colour and chemical resistance differ.

63
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:36,444
EPW-P:

64
00:02:36,444 --> 00:02:37,333
potable water.

65
00:02:37,333 --> 00:02:37,778
EPW-S:

66
00:02:37,778 --> 00:02:40,000
sewage, chemicals, oils and fuel.

67
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Zone E:

68
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,500
joints and penetrations.

69
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:46,500
Joints and penetrations are where water finds a path.

70
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:47,667
Candidate products:

71
00:02:47,667 --> 00:02:50,000
Hydrostop HW, Hyperseal DP-2010H.

72
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:56,000
A PVC waterstop is cast across the joint.

73
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,636
Tie waterstops to reinforcement;

74
00:02:57,636 --> 00:03:00,500
allow 24 hours after bonding before pouring.

75
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:06,000
Different tests, so each product is shown as reported.

76
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:06,409
HW:

77
00:03:06,409 --> 00:03:08,455
hollow bulb for expansion joints.

78
00:03:08,455 --> 00:03:08,864
DP-2010H:

79
00:03:08,864 --> 00:03:10,500
not for expansion joints.

80
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:11,333
Zone F:

81
00:03:11,333 --> 00:03:13,000
façades and exposed concrete.

82
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Exposed concrete faces carbon dioxide, rain and sun.

83
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:17,800
Candidate products:

84
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:21,000
Repcoat, Repcoat FF, Repcoat FF Plus, Repcoat S.

85
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:27,000
Primer first, then Repcoat at the stated rate per coat.

86
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,800
Wait for the primer;

87
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:31,500
two coats on dark, absorbent surfaces.

88
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:35,000
Carbonation is tested differently, so no bars.

89
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,000
Missing data is tagged.

90
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:37,417
Repcoat:

91
00:03:37,417 --> 00:03:38,250
high-build elastomeric.

92
00:03:38,250 --> 00:03:38,667
FF:

93
00:03:38,667 --> 00:03:39,500
matt finish.

94
00:03:39,500 --> 00:03:40,333
Zone G:

95
00:03:40,333 --> 00:03:42,000
steel and industrial exposure.

96
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Industrial exposure adds chemicals.

97
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:46,875
Candidate products:

98
00:03:46,875 --> 00:03:49,500
Strongcoat EN100, Strongcoat EPW-S, Repcoat P.

99
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:50,100
EN100:

100
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:55,500
base coat and topcoat on prepared concrete or steel.

101
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:58,200
Base coat at the stated rate;

102
00:03:58,200 --> 00:04:00,000
no primer unless porous.

103
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:05,500
Bond strength uses the same method for all three.

104
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:05,929
EN100:

105
00:04:05,929 --> 00:04:06,786
chemical resistance.

106
00:04:06,786 --> 00:04:07,643
Repcoat P:

107
00:04:07,643 --> 00:04:08,500
UV resistance.

108
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:12,500
The matrix shows where each data sheet lists a use.

109
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:17,043
A tick appears only where the data sheet lists that use.

110
00:04:17,043 --> 00:04:22,000
Where the sheet lists other uses, they appear in the last column.

111
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Always check the data sheet and your project conditions before you specify.

112
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,083
HPD and VOC data available.

113
00:04:32,083 --> 00:04:33,333
EPD on request.

114
00:04:33,333 --> 00:04:37,500
Third-party testing when a project or CE mark requires it.

115
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:42,500
Don Construction Products.

